From 6a799c5b56895f9404769fef5dcb3034c7ec66d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:25:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] serial: stm32: wake up runtime device before deep suspend

If the device is already in a runtime suspended state when
pm_runtime_force_suspend() is called:
- stm32_usart_runtime_suspend() will not be called
- stm32_usart_runtime_resume() will also not be called

Not calling stm32_usart_runtime_resume() causes an issue when waking up
from deep low-power mode, because the RXNEIE bit will not be set again
after being cleared by the interrupt routine during the next deep
low-power sequence.

To avoid that, make sure the device is in a runtime active state before
continuing the deep suspend routine.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Iba24ecf4c54b3c95c376449cb33fc54ab0838623
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/600874
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c b/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
index 6992cfc4fcde..14e784a4c5fb 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
@@ -2481,6 +2481,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused stm32_usart_serial_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 
 	if (device_may_wakeup(dev) || device_wakeup_path(dev)) {
+		pm_runtime_get_sync(port->dev);
+
 		ret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
@@ -2526,6 +2528,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused stm32_usart_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
 		ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
+
+		pm_runtime_put_sync_autosuspend(port->dev);
 	}
 
 	ret = uart_resume_port(&stm32_usart_driver, port);
-- 
